    <h2 class="aatp-h2">How does AgeAura Pure NMN + TMG work?</h2>
    <div class="aatp-prose">
      <p>If you've been reading the longevity literature, you already know the story: <strong>NAD⁺ levels decline as we age.</strong> NAD⁺ is the cofactor your mitochondria use to make energy and the molecule your sirtuins depend on for cellular maintenance. Less NAD⁺ means slower repair, slower metabolism, and the familiar "feeling older than I should."</p>
      <p>NMN (nicotinamide mononucleotide) is a direct NAD⁺ precursor. But here's what most single-ingredient NMN products quietly skip: the body uses <strong>methyl groups</strong> every time it processes NMN. Take NMN alone, long enough, and you can deplete the very methyl pool your body needs for everything from neurotransmitter synthesis to DNA stability.</p>
      <p><strong>That's where TMG comes in.</strong> TMG (trimethylglycine, also called betaine) is one of the body's most efficient methyl donors. Pairing 100&nbsp;mg of TMG with 200&nbsp;mg of NMN is the protocol Dr. David Sinclair himself has spoken about publicly — and the one that the most informed biohackers have been quietly building out of two separate bottles.</p>
      <p style="font-weight:600">AgeAura puts them in one capsule, at a daily dose that costs less than your morning coffee.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

